\begin{abstract}
The \software{hep-font} package sets up the text fonts for the HEP package suite.
It keeps or sets the document font size, switches between serif and sans-serif documents, chooses lining or oldstyle numerals, and provides Greek letters in text.
With \hologo{pdfLaTeX} it uses \LM extended by \CM shapes, with \hologo{LuaLaTeX} and \hologo{XeLaTeX} it uses \NCM.
The package configures text only; the matching math fonts are provided by the \software{hep-math-font} package.
\end{abstract}

The package is loaded using "\usepackage{hep-font}".
When the \software{hep-math-font} package is used as well, it has to be loaded after this package.

\section{Options}

\DescribeMacro{size}
The "size="\meta{size} option sets the document font size, for example "size=10.5pt", using the \software{fontsize} package.
The default "size=default" keeps the font size chosen by the document class.
Sizes that are not positive point sizes are reported as errors.

\DescribeMacro{sans}
\DescribeMacro{serif}
The "sans" option switches the main text to the sans-serif font, the default "serif" option keeps the serif font.

\DescribeMacro{oldstyle}
\DescribeMacro{lining}
The "oldstyle" option switches to oldstyle numerals such as 123 in text mode instead of the default lining numerals such as \textl{123}.
Numerals in math mode are always lining.

\section{Fonts}

The fonts depend on the engine, see \cref{tab:fonts}.
\begin{table}
\begin{tabular}{@{}l>{\raggedright}p{.36\linewidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{.36\linewidth}@{}}
\toprule
Role & \hologo{pdfLaTeX} & \hologo{LuaLaTeX} and \hologo{XeLaTeX} \\
\midrule
Text & \LM via \software{cfr-lm} & \NCM roman, sans and mono \\
Greek & CB Greek via \LGR & \NCM \\
Small caps & \CM bold and sans small caps & \NCM \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Text fonts used by the different engines.}
\label{tab:fonts}
\end{table}

For \hologo{pdfLaTeX} the "T1" and \LGR font encodings are loaded with the \software{fontenc} package \cite{fontenc}, together with the \software{inputenc} package \cite{inputenc} and the "utf8" option.
The \LM fonts are loaded using the \software{cfr-lm} package \cite{cfr-lm}, which extends the \LaTeX{} \NFSS with the \software{nfssext-cfr} package \cite{nfssext-cfr}.
Some restrictions of \CM fonts are lifted with the \software{fix-cm} package \cite{fix-cm} and the text companion fonts are loaded \cite{textcomp}.

\DescribeMacro{\textsc}
Bold \textbf{\textsc{Small Caps}} and sans-serif \textsf{\textsc{Small Caps}} are taken from the \CM fonts \cite{cm}, using the \software{sansmathfonts} \cite{sansmathfonts}, \software{hfoldsty} \cite{hfoldsty} and \software{slantsc} \cite{slantsc} packages.

\DescribeMacro{\textui}
A sans-serif upright italic font is provided using the \software{sansmathfonts} package \cite{sansmathfonts}.

For \hologo{LuaLaTeX} and \hologo{XeLaTeX} the \NCM text fonts are loaded with the \software{fontspec} package \cite{fontspec}.
Below \unit[9]{pt} the optical sizes designed for \unit[8]{pt} are used.
Slanted roman and typewriter text uses synthetic slanting, as the \software{fontsetup} package \cite{fontsetup} did previously.
\DescribeMacro{\uncial}
\DescribeMacro{\textuncial}
The uncial font is available via "\uncial" and "\textuncial"\marg{text}.

In both cases the \software{microtype} \cite{microtype} optimisations are activated.

\section{Macros}

\DescribeMacro{\textl}
\DescribeMacro{\texto}
\DescribeMacro{\textp}
\DescribeMacro{\textt}
The numeral style can be changed locally with "\textl"\marg{text} for lining, "\texto"\marg{text} for oldstyle, "\textp"\marg{text} for proportional and "\textt"\marg{text} for tabular numerals.
\DescribeMacro{\textpl}
\DescribeMacro{\textpo}
\DescribeMacro{\texttl}
\DescribeMacro{\textto}
The combinations are available as "\textpl", "\textpo", "\texttl" and "\textto".
\DescribeMacro{\lstyle}
\DescribeMacro{\ostyle}
\DescribeMacro{\pstyle}
\DescribeMacro{\tstyle}
The corresponding declarations are "\lstyle", "\ostyle", "\pstyle", "\tstyle", "\plstyle", "\postyle", "\tlstyle" and "\tostyle".

\DescribeMacro{\tmstyle}
\DescribeMacro{\tvstyle}
The "\tmstyle" declaration selects the usual fixed-width typewriter font and "\tvstyle" selects the proportional \LM typewriter font.
With \hologo{LuaLaTeX} and \hologo{XeLaTeX} the proportional typewriter font does not contain Greek letters.

\DescribeMacro{\codestyle}
\DescribeMacro{\code}
The "\codestyle" declaration selects fixed-width typewriter with lining numerals and is used for verbatim text.
The "\code"\marg{code} macro typesets its argument verbatim in this style.

\DescribeMacro{\alpha}
Greek letters such as "\alpha" and "\Gamma" typeset text Greek outside of math, using the \software{alphabeta} package \cite{alphabeta}, \eg \alpha\beta\Gamma.
In math mode they keep their usual meaning.
Hyphenation and other language settings are left to language packages.

\DescribeMacro{\tableofcontents}
Entries of the \TOC, tabulars and equation numbers use tabular numerals, which are lining or oldstyle like the numerals of the text.
Tabulars are covered whether they are inside a float or not, while float captions keep the proportional numerals of the text.
With \hologo{XeLaTeX} the regular and italic serif faces of \NCM keep proportional oldstyle numerals, since the order of their OpenType features cannot be changed there.
The equation counter itself is not changed, so that references and hyperlinks are unaffected.

The macros can be used in sectioning titles together with the \software{hyperref} package \cite{hyperref}.
Its bookmarks keep the argument of the text commands such as "\textl" and ignore the declarations such as "\ostyle", and the Greek letters become Unicode characters.
In bookmarks and document information "\code" keeps its argument as it is, including underscores, but as a verbatim command it cannot be used in sectioning titles.

