# The `hep-font` package

Latin Modern and New Computer Modern text fonts with numeral styles
and Greek letters

## Introduction

The `hep-font` package sets up the text fonts for the HEP package suite.
It keeps or sets the document font size, switches between serif and
sans-serif documents, chooses lining or oldstyle numerals, and provides
Greek letters in text. With pdfLaTeX it uses Latin Modern extended by
Computer Modern shapes, with LuaLaTeX and XeLaTeX it uses New Computer
Modern. The matching math fonts are provided by the `hep-math-font`
package.

The package is loaded using `\usepackage{hep-font}`.

